    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel: Denial of Service in qla2xxx SCSI driver due to improper command handling after chip reset (CVE-2025-68745)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: 6fire: fix use-after-free on disconnect (CVE-2026-31581)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nfnetlink_cthelper: fix OOB read in nfnl_cthelper_dump_table() (CVE-2026-43450)\n\n* kernel: crypto: pcrypt - Fix handling of MAY_BACKLOG requests (CVE-2026-43493)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh pointer after ipv6_hop_jumbo() (CVE-2026-63924)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh after handling HAO option (CVE-2026-63922)\n\n* kernel: ipv6: validate extension header length before copying to cmsg (CVE-2026-63920)\n\n* kernel: kernel: strparser: use-after-free via msg_timer_work rearm after strp_done() cancellation ()\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
